      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This seems to work properly in the editor with a small patch to CalcVelocityAtPoint,\n\nbefore\n\n```\n\nfloat3 tangent = math.cross(math.normalize(x), this.angularNormal);\n\nvelocity += tangent * math.length(x) * (this.angularSpeed * ((float) Math.PI / 180f));\n\n```\n\nafter\n\n```\n\nvelocity += math.cross(x, this.angularNormal) * (this.angularSpeed * ((float) Math.PI / 180f))\n\n```\n\nmath.normalize(0) returns Nan. Rather than pulling out the offset vector and length separately, using it as is non-normalized makes the math work out properly.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
