  "details": "If a sender is 0 radius, it shows 0 for the velocity components in advanced parameters of any receiver. Oddly, this works properly if the sender is not currently rotating AT ALL. However, if there is any angular momentum (even due to floating point error), the math fails and the velocity is calculated as NaN (getting exposed to the parameters as 0).",
